== Reward ==

<ul><li>  {{:Deck of Spontaneous Generation}}
<li> ... and many other items ([[#Rewards|see below]])
</ul>

== Part 1: Acquiring the Deck ==

This quest is given by [[Ferjeneror]], but you can start in the Dining Room before moving on to the Hedge Maze.

=== King Cod Card ===
There is a level 1 ogre named [[Dinner]] on the table of the Dining Room. Kill Dinner to loot the [[King Cod Card]]. Be cautious when going to loot the card as there are two level 55 wizards perma-rooted to the chandelier above him. They are scowling to everyone and like to chain ice comets together. They cannot be hit by melee attacks and will not chase when aggroed. It's wise to use [[Harmony]] or [[Calm]] before entering, or simply moving very quickly.

=== Colored Cod Cards ===
Alternatively, you can [[Skill Fishing|fish]] in the castle moat for the four colored cod cards: {{:Black Cod Card}}, {{:Blue Cod Card}}, {{:Red Cod Card}}, and {{:White Cod Card}}.  You can turn these four cards in instead of the {{:King Cod Card}}.

=== Reward ===
After looting the card(s) head to the flower maze and turn in your King Cod Card or all four colored cod cards to the sphinx named [[Ferjeneror]] to get your:

<ul><li> {{:Deck of Spontaneous Generation}}
</ul>

== Part 2: Using the Deck of Spontaneous Generation ==

Throughout the Plane of Mischief, various Mobs drop [[:Category:Plane_of_Mischief_Cards|playing cards]].  [[:Category:Plane_of_Mischief_Cards#Where_Can_Cards_be_Found.3F|Collect these cards]] and combine them in the {{:Deck of Spontaneous Generation}}, with each combination generating a different reward.

=== Rewards ===

Note that every item here except the {{:Black Flower of Functionality}}, {{:Green Flower of Functionality}}, and {{:White Flower of Functionality}} require at least one Throne card.

===== Armor of Distraction =====

These [[Armor of Distraction|armor pieces]] are used in two different ways (together) to create [[Plane of Mischief Armor]].

First, they can be used in the [[The Gift Box]] quest (along with a [[Words of Wealth]]) to create [[The Gift Box|gift boxes]], which generate [[:Category:Plane of Mischief Dolls|Plane of Mischief dolls]].  Second, those [[:Category:Plane of Mischief Dolls|dolls]] can be combined with (still more) [[Armor of Distraction|armor pieces]] in the [[Plane of Mischief Armor Quest]] to create [[Plane of Mischief Armor]].

Note that every armor piece requires two thrones except the {{:Vambraces of Distraction}} (which require only one).  Because the gift boxes to generate the [[:Category:Plane of Mischief Dolls|dolls]] require a ''minimum'' of two thrones to generate, every armor piece except the {{:Vambraces of Distraction}} requires at least four throne cards ... and remember, gift boxes are random, so it could take many more unless you trade with other players or are very lucky.

